1,2$ Basidiomata persistently white; apices generally simple; basidiospores sometimes longer than 10 mm on average ..
1,3$ Basidiomata pinkish or with grey colour in age; apices cristate to simple; basidiospores always smaller than 10 mm on average ..
2,0$ (1) Basidiomata simple to sparsely branched (b.r. 0-2); apices sometimes subcristate . . $ rugosa (R2)
2,0$ Basidiomata profusely branched (b.r. 3-5); apices simple . $ aff. rugosa (R1)
3,0$ (1) Basidiomata white or pale grey in the branches with age; stipe generally not well-delimited due to the basitonic branching $ cristata (C3)
3,4$ Basidiomata dark grey with age; stipe well-delimited or not, branching acrotonic or basitonic .
